---
import Prose from "../layouts/Prose.astro";
import { SITE_REPO, SITE_HOST } from "../consts";

const title = "Privacy";
const description =
  "What jostraca.org collects, what it does not, and who processes the " +
  "request when you read a page.";
---

<Prose
  title={title}
  description={description}
  lede="This is a documentation site. It has no accounts, no forms and no cookies, and it asks you for nothing."
>
  <h2 id="collect">What this site collects</h2>

  <p>
    Nothing you type, because there is nothing to type into. There is no sign-up,
    no login, no comment box, no newsletter, and no contact form anywhere on
    {SITE_HOST}. The site sets no cookies and writes nothing to your browser's
    storage. You can read every page, and every page's markdown twin, without
    identifying yourself in any way.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hosting">Who serves the pages</h2>

  <p>
    The site runs on Cloudflare Workers. Delivering a page necessarily means
    Cloudflare handles the request, and in doing so it processes the usual
    request metadata -  your IP address, the URL you asked for, your user agent -
    to route the response and to protect the service from abuse. Cloudflare
    retains request-level logs for a limited period as part of running the
    platform. That processing is Cloudflare's, under its own terms; this site
    neither adds to it nor receives a copy of it in any identifiable form.
  </p>

  <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>

  <p>
    The site is built to support Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is cookieless
    and collects aggregate page-view data without a device identifier and
    without tracking you across other sites. It is enabled only when a beacon
    token is configured at build time; when it is not, the script is not
    included in the page at all. If you want to know which state the live site
    is in, read the page source and look for a
    <code>cloudflareinsights.com</code> script tag -  its presence or absence is
    the whole answer, and it is not something this page can be stale about.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-parties">Third parties</h2>

  <p>
    No third-party fonts, no analytics beyond what this page lists, no tag manager, no
    embedded video, no advertising, and no social widgets. Every stylesheet,
    script and font this site uses is served from its own domain, so reading a
    page does not quietly issue requests to anyone else. Links that leave the
    site -  to GitHub, npm, pkg.go.dev -  are ordinary links, and they take you to
    services with their own privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your data, and questions about it</h2>

  <p>
    Because the site holds no personal data of yours, there is nothing here to
    export, correct, or delete. If you have a question about what Cloudflare
    processes on the way to you, its documentation covers that in detail. If you
    believe something on this site contradicts what is written here, that is a
    bug and is worth reporting on
    <a href={SITE_REPO} rel="noopener">the site repository</a>.
  </p>

  <p class="footnote">
    This page describes the site, not the Jostraca software. The generator runs
    entirely on your own machine, sends nothing anywhere, and has no telemetry
    of any kind. Last reviewed against the code on this page's own build.
  </p>
</Prose>
